IMPORT prelude

-- Civil Law Act 1909 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 15/10/2024)
-- LAYER 1 -- THE NOUNS: the kinds of thing the Act names, as choices from a list.
-- Nouns only: no rule, no #EVAL.  Every constructor name is chosen not to collide with a name in
-- the copied Interpretation Act modules (Days, Weeks, Months, Years, From, After, Moment, Means, Includes, Definition...).
-- The membership test: could a witness of ordinary competence testify to this fact, or does answering it need the Act?
-- Only the first kind is here.  Whether a kind makes a contract void or a claim survive is a rule, in the module of the section.

§ `Section 4 -- kinds of administration and of tenant`

-- s 4(1): the two situations in which the bankruptcy rules are applied.
DECLARE `Kind of insolvent administration` IS ONE OF
    `Administration by a court of a deceased person's estate that proves insufficient to pay debts and liabilities in full`
    `Winding up of a company under the Insolvency Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 whose assets prove insufficient`
    `Another kind of administration`

-- s 4(3): who is forbidden to commit voluntary waste.
DECLARE `Kind of tenant` IS ONE OF
    `Tenant for life or lives`
    `Leasehold tenant`
    `Another kind of occupier`

-- s 4(4): what the Act says a "leasehold tenant" includes.
DECLARE `Kind of leasehold tenancy` IS ONE OF
    `Tenancy for a term`
    `Periodical tenancy`
    `Tenancy at will`
    `Another kind of tenancy`

§ `Section 5 -- gaming and wagering, funding of claims`

-- s 5(3A): the six heads of exception to the nullity of gaming and wagering contracts.
DECLARE `Kind of contract within the exceptions of section 5(3A)` IS ONE OF
    `Gaming under the control or supervision of a person or organisation exempted under the repealed Common Gaming Houses Act 1961`
    `Betting held or run by a person or organisation exempted under the repealed Betting Act 1960`
    `Gaming wagering or betting using remote communication run by an exempt operator or exempted person under the repealed Remote Gambling Act 2014`
    `Betting on a totalisator run by or for the Singapore Totalisator Board or a turf club under an approved scheme`
    `A private lottery run by the holder of a permit under the repealed Private Lotteries Act 2011`
    `Gaming wagering or betting run by a licensee or other person under the Gambling Control Act 2022`
    `None of these kinds`

-- s 5(5): the heads of "investment activity".
DECLARE `Kind of activity under section 5(5)` IS ONE OF
    `Contract or option for the future delivery of securities commodity currency or a financial instrument`
    `Contract or option entered into with the intention of settling differences in prices or values`
    `Exchange or grant of an option for the exchange of securities commodity currency or a financial instrument`
    `Transaction in securities commodity currency or a financial instrument`
    `Grant of a right or option relating to an obligation to pay interest or to exchange obligations to pay interest`
    `Contract or option to pay the difference between a pre-agreed interest rate and the prevailing rate`
    `Securities futures contract or derivative listed or traded on an exchange outside Singapore`
    `Any other derivative including a swap cap collar or floor`
    `Another activity`

§ `Section 6 -- the five kinds of action that need a signed writing, and immovable property`

-- s 6(a) to (e).
DECLARE `Kind of action under section 6` IS ONE OF
    `Action on a special promise by an executor or administrator to answer damages out of his own estate`
    `Action on a special promise to answer for the debt default or miscarriage of another person`
    `Action on an agreement made upon consideration of marriage`
    `Action on a contract for the sale or other disposition of immovable property or an interest in it`
    `Action on an agreement not to be performed within one year of its making`
    `Another kind of action`

-- s 6(d), s 7(1): what the thing concerned is, in the words of the Interpretation Act definition of "immovable property".
DECLARE `Kind of property` IS ONE OF
    Land
    `A benefit to arise out of land`
    `A thing attached to the earth`
    `A thing permanently fastened to anything attached to the earth`
    `Some other kind of property`

§ `Section 9 -- the euro`

-- s 9(1): how the euro is used in place of the substituted currency or the Ecu.
DECLARE `Use of the euro under section 9(1)` IS ONE OF
    `Used in determining the value of the currency or of the Ecu`
    `Tendered`
    `Used in another way`

-- s 9(2): in what currency performance is offered.
DECLARE `Currency of performance` IS ONE OF
    `The currency originally designated in the instrument and still legal tender`
    `The currency originally designated in the instrument but no longer legal tender`
    `The euro`
    `Any other currency`

-- s 9(3): the events that do not discharge or excuse performance.
DECLARE `Event under section 9(3)` IS ONE OF
    `The introduction of the euro`
    `The tendering of euros in compliance with section 9(1)(a) or (b)`
    `The determining of the value of an obligation in compliance with section 9(1)(a) or (b)`
    `Calculating or determining the subject or medium of payment with reference to a basis substituted or replaced due to the introduction of the euro`
    `Another event`

§ `Section 10 -- survival of causes of action`

-- s 10(2) and s 10(3)(b): the kind of cause of action.
DECLARE `Kind of cause of action` IS ONE OF
    Defamation
    Seduction
    `Inducing one spouse to leave or remain apart from the other`
    `A claim for damages on the ground of adultery`
    `A claim for breach of promise to marry`
    `Another cause of action`

-- s 10(3)(a): the head of damages.
DECLARE `Head of damages for the benefit of an estate` IS ONE OF
    `Exemplary damages`
    `Damages for loss of income in respect of a period after the death`
    `Another head of damages`

§ `Sections 20 to 22 -- death caused by a wrongful act`

-- s 20(8): how the person is related to the deceased.
DECLARE `Relationship to the deceased` IS ONE OF
    `The wife or husband of the deceased`
    `The former wife of the deceased`
    `A parent grandparent or great-grandparent of the deceased`
    `A child grandchild or great-grandchild of the deceased`
    `A person not a child of the deceased treated by the deceased as a child of the family in a marriage to which the deceased was a party`
    `A person who is a brother sister uncle or aunt of the deceased`
    `A person who is the issue of a brother sister uncle or aunt of the deceased`
    `Another relationship`

-- s 20(9): the footing on which the relationship is deduced.
DECLARE `Basis of the relationship` IS ONE OF
    `By blood`
    `By adoption by the person concerned`
    `By adoption into the family of someone else`
    `By affinity`
    `Of the half blood`
    `As a stepchild`
    `As an illegitimate child of its mother or reputed father`

-- s 20(10): the kinds of adoption the Act counts.
DECLARE `Kind of adoption` IS ONE OF
    `Adoption order under the Adoption of Children Act 2022`
    `Adoption order under a corresponding previous written law`
    `Adoption recognised as valid by the law of Singapore`
    `Another kind of adoption`

-- s 21(2): who may claim damages for bereavement.
DECLARE `Class of claimant for bereavement` IS ONE OF
    `Surviving wife or husband of the deceased`
    `Surviving child of the deceased`
    `Surviving parent of the deceased or mother if the deceased was illegitimate`
    `Person who during a marriage treated the deceased minor as a child of the family`
    `Surviving brother or sister of the deceased`
    `Not in any of these classes`

-- s 22(1) and (3): items in assessing damages.
DECLARE `Item in assessing damages under section 22` IS ONE OF
    `A sum paid or payable under a contract of assurance or insurance`
    `A sum payable under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953`
    `A pension or gratuity paid or payable as a result of the death`
    `The remarriage or prospect of remarriage of a widow`
    `Another item`

§ `Sections 31 and 32 -- accumulation and perpetuities`

-- s 31(2): the periods for which a pre-2004 settlement may accumulate income.
DECLARE `Period of accumulation` IS ONE OF
    `The life of the grantor or settlor`
    `A term of 21 years from the death of the grantor settlor or testator`
    `The minority of persons living or en ventre sa mere at the death of the grantor settlor or testator`
    `The minority only of persons who would for the time being if of full age be entitled to the income`
    `A term of 21 years from the date of the making of the disposition`
    `The minority of persons in being at the date of the making of the disposition`
    `None of these periods`

§ `Sections 35 and 36 -- minors of 18 and over`

-- s 35(4) and (5)(b): the kind of contract.
DECLARE `Kind of contract by a minor who has attained 18` IS ONE OF
    `Contract for the sale purchase mortgage assignment or settlement of land`
    `Contract for a lease of land not exceeding 3 years`
    `Contract for a lease of land for more than 3 years`
    `Contract by which the minor's beneficial interest under a trust is sold transferred or pledged`
    `Contract for the settlement of legal proceedings in which the minor is under disability on account of age`
    `Contract for the settlement of a claim from which such proceedings may arise`
    `Contract extinguishing a trust or varying its terms`
    `Another kind of contract`

-- The Schedule, paragraphs 1 to 5.
DECLARE `Kind of legal proceeding or action` IS ONE OF
    `Proceeding arising from a contract that has effect under section 35 as if the minor were of full age`
    `Proceeding arising from the minor acting as a director of a company`
    `Proceeding arising from the minor acting as a manager of a limited liability partnership`
    `Proceeding arising from a bill of exchange drawn or indorsed by the minor`
    `Proceeding arising from a bill of exchange drawn or indorsed by another person in favour of the minor`
    `Proceeding arising from the carrying on of a business by a minor registered under the Business Names Registration Act 2014`
    `Proceeding arising from the carrying on of business by a minor as a partner in a limited partnership registered under the Limited Partnerships Act 2008`
    `Proceeding arising from the minor acting as a person responsible for the management of a limited partnership business`
    `Another proceeding`

§ `The parties and acts of the regulative rules`

-- s 4(3): the tenant who shall not commit voluntary waste.
DECLARE `Party under section 4(3)` IS ONE OF
    `The tenant for life or leasehold tenant`

DECLARE `Act under section 4(3)` IS ONE OF
    `commit voluntary waste`

-- s 5B(3): the qualifying Third-Party Funder and the funded party, who must comply with the prescribed requirements.
DECLARE `Party under section 5B(3)` IS ONE OF
    `The qualifying Third-Party Funder`
    `The funded party`

DECLARE `Act under section 5B(3)` IS ONE OF
    `comply with the requirements prescribed for the third-party funding contract and ensure that they are complied with`

-- s 20(3), (4) and (6): who brings the action for wrongful death and what the claimant must deliver.
DECLARE `Party under section 20` IS ONE OF
    `The executor or administrator of the deceased`
    `A person for whose benefit the action could have been brought`
    `The claimant in an action under section 20`

DECLARE `Act under section 20` IS ONE OF
    `bring the action by and in the name of the executor or administrator`
    `bring the action by and in the name of the persons for whose benefit it could have been brought`
    `deliver full particulars to the defendant or his solicitor`

-- s 28(5): the subtenant who must give notice of the claim to his immediate landlord.
DECLARE `Party under section 28(5)` IS ONE OF
    `The subtenant`

DECLARE `Act under section 28(5)` IS ONE OF
    `give notice of the originating claim to his immediate landlord`
